localtest: the inbox's links to the Access Management GUI (the menu's access management link, a dialog's "who has
access", the profile's settings and Altinn 2 links, and the party switch through reportee/changeandredirect) go to
am.ui.<public host> on the page's port when the inbox runs on af.<public host> over http, the stack's
access-management group (task 68). Upstream maps every host it does not know to prod (am.ui.altinn.no). With the group
off, the front door answers that host with its 503 naming the group. The stack is plain http, which keeps the rule off
any deployed inbox.
Against Altinn/dialogporten-frontend bb74dff2c425f2aff48759ed9c6370e73436545d. Both Dockerfiles apply every patch in their source stage (git apply).

--- a/packages/frontend/src/auth/url.ts
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/auth/url.ts
@@ -68,6 +68,13 @@ export const getEnvByHost = (): hostEnv => {
   return 'prod';
 };
 
+// localtest: on af.<public host> over http the Access Management GUI is am.ui.<public host> on the same port (the stack's
